Patch 15: promote transform-statistics pruning to speed 2.

Standalone. Independent of GPT patch 0001 (which promotes the same feature to
speed 3); the two compose, since this adds the assignment at speed 2 and speed
features cascade upward.

This feature is the only one in the set measured at two presets:

    speed 4   +4.90% time / +0.10% BD   ratio 49.0   (bar 20)  PASS
    speed 3   +6.12% time / +0.18% BD   ratio 34.0   (bar 25)  PASS

The speedup grew as the preset slowed, which is what a pruning feature should
do: the deeper the search it replaces, the more work it removes. Speed 2 is
deeper still.

I want to be explicit that I expect this arm to FAIL, and it is worth running
anyway.

The ratio fell from 49.0 to 34.0 across the first promotion, so BD-rate grew
faster than time saving did. A second promotion of similar character lands
around 25, while the speed-2 bar rises to 30. Extrapolating two points to a
third is exactly the reasoning that failed on this branch when the
stationarity margin was loosened a third time and collapsed from 26.7 to 14.7.

It is still worth one arm. The extrapolation assumes the two quantities keep
their ratio of growth, and they need not: the transform-type search at speed 2
is not merely a deeper version of speed 3's, it evaluates a wider type set, and
statistics-based pruning may remove proportionally more of it. That is a real
mechanism, not wishful arithmetic, and no cheaper experiment can settle it.

Run it as its own arm and expect to learn where the promotion curve turns over
rather than to win. -DAVM_S2_PRUNE_TX_STATS=0 disables it without a patch edit.

